# Utils extraction

Put reusable pure helpers and shared non-UI logic in [`utils/`](utils/), not inside React components or pages.

## What belongs in `utils/`

- String/number/date formatting and parsing (e.g. `getMonogram`)
- Pure transforms (shuffle, pick, id generation)
- Storage/key helpers, room code helpers, constants
- Anything with no JSX and no React hooks that can be reused or unit-tested alone

## What stays in the component

- Rendering, event handlers wired to UI, local UI state
- Thin wrappers that only call utils and pass props

## Conventions

- One focused module per concern: `utils/monogram.ts`, `utils/room-helpers.ts`
- Import via `@/utils/...`
- Prefer named exports
- Do not put shadcn/`cn` helpers here — those stay in `@/lib/utils`

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — helper buried in a component file
function getMonogram(name: string) { /* ... */ }

export function CharacterCard() {
  const monogram = getMonogram(character.name);
  // ...
}

// ✅ GOOD — helper in utils, component only renders
import { getMonogram } from "@/utils/monogram";

export function CharacterCard() {
  const monogram = getMonogram(character.name);
  // ...
}
```
